    <string id="pf_irc_encyclopedia_pripyat4"><text>Pripyat-4</text></string>
    <string id="pf_irc_encyclopedia_pripyat4_text"><text>%c[255,170,220,255]Chat with real players%c[default]\n“Pripyat-4” is the PDA section for communicating with other real players. The shared channel and private dialogs use IRC.\n\n%c[255,170,220,255]What is IRC?%c[default]\nIRC (Internet Relay Chat) is a simple network protocol for exchanging text messages in shared channels and private dialogs. The game interface hides the connection details: for ordinary use, enter a nickname and authorize.\n\n%c[255,170,220,255]Notifications%c[default]\nThe “Pripyat-4” settings let you independently enable or disable notification display and sound for shared-channel messages, and for private messages and @nickname mentions. While the chat page is open, redundant shared-channel notification sounds are suppressed.\n\n%c[255,170,220,255]Local correspondence%c[default]\nShared-channel and private-dialog history is stored outside game saves at the relative path:\n%c[255,120,210,120]userdata\pf_irc_chat\history.txt%c[default]\n\nThis path is relative to the game root. History persists through quick loads and game restarts.</text></string>
